<section class="section">
	<div class="section-inner section-inner-pt-xs section-inner-pb-xs">
		<div class="container-narrow">
			<div class="c-content-right">
				<h2 class="u-a2 js-animated-stagger-element">
					For activities on the mainland part of the island, we recommend walking and hiking along
					the numerous trails. Additionally, in Pomena, you can rent almost anything you can think
					of, from bicycles, kayaks, scooters, to buggies.
				</h2>

				<div class="c-content-right__description js-animated-stagger-element">
					<p>
						For those more active, Mljet is abundant with gravel country roads, perfect for cycling,
						as well as asphalted roads, ideal for scenic drives with your family and children. Rent
						a kayak or canoe and make your vacation unforgettable by paddling on the pristine waters
						of the Small and Big Lakes within the untouched nature of the national park. After your
						ride, be sure to leave some time to pass through the channel under the Little Bridge,
						especially if you have children.
					</p>
					<p>
						If you are a spelunking enthusiast, Mljet is rich in numerous caves, and we especially
						recommend visiting the geomorphological phenomenon, Odysseus' Cave near Babino Polje on
						the southern side of the island, which is also perfect for exploration along with
						numerous underwater caves and the stunning marine world, ideal for diving enthusiasts.
					</p>
					<p>
						And at the end of the day, wherever you are on the island, whether you are an adventurer
						or not, don't forget to pause and enjoy the magnificent sunsets and experience the
						unique power and beauty of the island of Mljet.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
